# Deploy → go live

When the user says **"deploy"** (or similar: "commit these changes", "commit and deploy", "ship it", "push live", "go live"), run the full deploy pipeline in one turn.

## Pipeline (always in this order)

1. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` — understand what will ship; draft an accurate commit message if committing.
2. **Commit** if there are staged or unstaged changes worth shipping (never commit secrets).
3. **Push** immediately after a successful commit, or push existing commits if the branch is ahead and working tree is clean:
   ```bash
   git push origin HEAD
   ```
4. Verify with `git status` — branch must not be "ahead of origin".
5. Confirm to the user: **changes are pushed and Vercel will deploy live** (typically ~1 min).

## Trigger phrases

- **"deploy"** ← primary
- "commit these changes"
- "commit and deploy" / "ship it" / "push live" / "go live"

## Do NOT push when

- User says "commit but don't push" or "local commit only"
- Commit failed or pre-commit hook rejected it
- Nothing to commit **and** branch is not ahead of origin (tell user they're already synced)

## If push fails

- Show the error; never ask for tokens in chat.
- User can re-auth once in terminal: `git push origin HEAD`

## Vercel (how deploy works)

- Production deploys are triggered by **push to `main` on GitHub** when the repo is linked in the [Vercel dashboard](https://vercel.com/dashboard).
- No local `vercel` CLI or `.vercel/` folder is required for that flow.
- This project uses `@vercel/analytics`; ensure the Vercel project is connected to `GyanDevs/My-Portfolio`.
